{"id":"d2ed815720a23b5c","group":"27","path":"27/27-thm-selfdualextensionbijection.md","title":"Bijection induced by self-dual extension","display":"thm-selfdualextensionbijection — Bijection induced by self-dual extension","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Boolean Functions: Theory, Algorithms, and Applications","book_abbrev":"27","label":"27-thm-selfdualextensionbijection","aliases":["27-thm-selfdualextensionbijection"],"display":"thm-selfdualextensionbijection — Bijection induced by self-dual extension","depends_on":["[[27-df-selfdualextension]]","[[27-df-selfdual]]"],"source_file":"C:\\Users\\lzy\\Documents\\BaiduSyncdisk\\calibre\\Yves Crama, Peter L. Hammer\\Boolean Functions_ Theory, Algorith (5073)\\Boolean Functions_ Theory, Algo - Yves Crama, Peter L. Hammer.pdf","source_pdf_sha256":"1f81062da95a70f9a4f89063cdedaaec08946ffbc117c7345baa7065770cfa1f","source_section":"§4.1.3 Theorem 4.14","source_printed_pages":"173","source_pdf_pages":"197","verification_status":"source-statement-checked-and-proved-in-note"},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Boolean Functions: Theory, Algorithms, and Applications"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"27"},{"key":"label","html":"27-thm-selfdualextensionbijection"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>27-thm-selfdualextensionbijection</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-selfdualextensionbijection — Bijection induced by self-dual extension"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"f9bd4987179e7e50\" href=\"?note=f9bd4987179e7e50\" title=\"27-df-selfdualextension\">27-df-selfdualextension</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"649b44626bd5cc6f\" href=\"?note=649b44626bd5cc6f\" title=\"27-df-selfdual\">27-df-selfdual</a></span></div>"},{"key":"source_file","html":"C:\\Users\\lzy\\Documents\\BaiduSyncdisk\\calibre\\Yves Crama, Peter L. Hammer\\Boolean Functions_ Theory, Algorith (5073)\\Boolean Functions_ Theory, Algo - Yves Crama, Peter L. Hammer.pdf"},{"key":"source_pdf_sha256","html":"1f81062da95a70f9a4f89063cdedaaec08946ffbc117c7345baa7065770cfa1f"},{"key":"source_section","html":"§4.1.3 Theorem 4.14"},{"key":"source_printed_pages","html":"173"},{"key":"source_pdf_pages","html":"197"},{"key":"verification_status","html":"source-statement-checked-and-proved-in-note"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\\in\\mathbb Z_{\\ge1}\">\\(n\\in\\mathbb Z_{\\ge1}\\)</span>，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{SD}_n\">\\(\\mathrm{SD}_n\\)</span> 见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"f9bd4987179e7e50\" href=\"?note=f9bd4987179e7e50\" title=\"27-df-selfdualextension\">27-df-selfdualextension</a>，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{SelfDual}_{n+1}\">\\(\\mathrm{SelfDual}_{n+1}\\)</span> 见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"649b44626bd5cc6f\" href=\"?note=649b44626bd5cc6f\" title=\"27-df-selfdual\">27-df-selfdual</a>。<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"B_n,B_{n+1}\">\\(B_n,B_{n+1}\\)</span> 与逆向限制映射 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"R_0\">\\(R_0\\)</span> 由下式构造。</p>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"B_r\\coloneqq\\{0,1\\}^{\\{0,1\\}^r}\\quad(r\\in\\{n,n+1\\}).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[B_r\\coloneqq\\{0,1\\}^{\\{0,1\\}^r}\\quad(r\\in\\{n,n+1\\}).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"R_0(g)\\coloneqq\\{(a,g(a\\cup\\{(n+1,0)\\}))\\mid a\\in\\{0,1\\}^n\\}\\quad(g\\in B_{n+1}).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[R_0(g)\\coloneqq\\{(a,g(a\\cup\\{(n+1,0)\\}))\\mid a\\in\\{0,1\\}^n\\}\\quad(g\\in B_{n+1}).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{SD}_n[B_n]=\\mathrm{SelfDual}_{n+1},\\qquad\\forall f\\in B_n\\;R_0(\\mathrm{SD}_n(f))=f,\\qquad\\forall g\\in\\mathrm{SelfDual}_{n+1}\\;\\mathrm{SD}_n(R_0(g))=g.\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{SD}_n[B_n]=\\mathrm{SelfDual}_{n+1},\\qquad\\forall f\\in B_n\\;R_0(\\mathrm{SD}_n(f))=f,\\qquad\\forall g\\in\\mathrm{SelfDual}_{n+1}\\;\\mathrm{SD}_n(R_0(g))=g.\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"|\\mathrm{SelfDual}_{n+1}|=2^{2^n}.\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[|\\mathrm{SelfDual}_{n+1}|=2^{2^n}.\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>补输入会交换选择位的两个分支，输出随之取补，因此 SD_n(f) 自对偶。限制到选择位 0 恢复 f，说明单射；任何自对偶 g 的选择位 1 分支都由选择位 0 分支唯一决定，说明满射。已核对原书双射证明及逆映射，不把扩充为 n+1 个变量说成在同一变量集上扩展真点集。</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"27-df-selfdualextension","status":"resolved","id":"f9bd4987179e7e50","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[27-df-selfdualextension]]","embed":false},{"target":"27-df-selfdual","status":"resolved","id":"649b44626bd5cc6f","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[27-df-selfdual]]","embed":false},{"target":"27-df-selfdualextension","status":"resolved","id":"f9bd4987179e7e50","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$n\\in\\mathbb Z_{\\ge1}$，$\\mathrm{SD}_n$ 见 [[27-df-selfdualextension]]，$\\mathrm{SelfDual}_{n+1}$ 见 [[27-df-selfdual]]。$B_n,B_{n+1}$ 与逆向限制映射 $R_0$ 由下式构造。","embed":false},{"target":"27-df-selfdual","status":"resolved","id":"649b44626bd5cc6f","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$n\\in\\mathbb Z_{\\ge1}$，$\\mathrm{SD}_n$ 见 [[27-df-selfdualextension]]，$\\mathrm{SelfDual}_{n+1}$ 见 [[27-df-selfdual]]。$B_n,B_{n+1}$ 与逆向限制映射 $R_0$ 由下式构造。","embed":false}],"attachments":[],"math":[{"tex":"n\\in\\mathbb Z_{\\ge1}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{SD}_n","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{SelfDual}_{n+1}","display":false},{"tex":"B_n,B_{n+1}","display":false},{"tex":"R_0","display":false},{"tex":"B_r\\coloneqq\\{0,1\\}^{\\{0,1\\}^r}\\quad(r\\in\\{n,n+1\\}).","display":true},{"tex":"R_0(g)\\coloneqq\\{(a,g(a\\cup\\{(n+1,0)\\}))\\mid a\\in\\{0,1\\}^n\\}\\quad(g\\in B_{n+1}).","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{SD}_n[B_n]=\\mathrm{SelfDual}_{n+1},\\qquad\\forall f\\in B_n\\;R_0(\\mathrm{SD}_n(f))=f,\\qquad\\forall g\\in\\mathrm{SelfDual}_{n+1}\\;\\mathrm{SD}_n(R_0(g))=g.","display":true},{"tex":"|\\mathrm{SelfDual}_{n+1}|=2^{2^n}.","display":true}],"bytes":1806,"backlinks":[{"id":"5244dbb38da17b8a","anchor":"ref-40","locations":["正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"[[27-thm-selfdualextensionbijection|thm-selfdualextensionbijection — Bijection induced by self-dual extension]]"}],"outgoing":["f9bd4987179e7e50","649b44626bd5cc6f"]}